{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Configure node1 as an NFSv4 server exporting /srv/nfs/shared to node2 and node3 over the dedicated storage network.","status":"satisfied","summary":"All nodes are on 10.100.143.0/24. Node1 actively exports /srv/nfs/shared with read-write access restricted to node2 and node3, serves NFS on port 2049, and remains active after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-13dd18a3773b4394","cmd-03e225a7eca741ef","cmd-952ef02101cc4bf4","cmd-7f86dd1d42f74fe2","cmd-b9d5919a1319451c","cmd-edb9d9f633414586"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Mount the exported directory at /mnt/shared on node2 and node3.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both clients show active NFSv4.2 mounts from node1 at /mnt/shared, with persistent fstab entries; the mounts recovered after client and server restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7255e9de21f541b7","cmd-4675e0dd4e674d22","cmd-163121d6469147dd","cmd-f74dc139699c425d","cmd-aa5f389254f94282","cmd-3e49255007f847ec"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Provide sharedops with UID and GID 4200 on all nodes and set the shared directory to sharedops:sharedops mode 2770.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct account lookups confirm sharedops UID/GID 4200 on all three nodes, and server and client observations show the shared directory owned by 4200:4200 with mode 2770.","evidence_ids":["cmd-cd78b94c57a84c2d","cmd-103188c0de2145e7","cmd-62da7cbe856b436c","cmd-b9d5919a1319451c","cmd-4675e0dd4e674d22","cmd-edb9d9f633414586"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Files created from either client are immediately available from the other while retaining ownership and permissions.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A node2-created file was immediately read on node3 with ownership 4200:4200 and mode 0660. A node3-created file was read and modified from node2 while retaining ownership 4200:4200 and mode 0750. Cross-client operation was also repeated successfully after all node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9c7a58447d82431c","cmd-6064bc11fabe4072","cmd-b21aa62e4caa444b","cmd-aa5f389254f94282","cmd-3e49255007f847ec"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Package installation, account and directory creation, export and mount configuration, test-file mutations, and restarts all directly supported implementation, bounded behavioral evidence, or the mandatory restart protocol. The initially incomplete export command still established required server prerequisites and was immediately corrected; the apparent file-test failure created a task-relevant test file and only failed because subsequent checks used an unprivileged identity. Neither represents unrelated residue. Final snapshots show healthy package state, no failed services, and only task-required NFS/RPC listeners. No abandoned temporary files or unrelated persistent changes are evidenced.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d0fc5b777fe44a26","cmd-2f6cae303d0842ae","cmd-4705b3a87e88468a","cmd-d6a2053ad74e45ca","cmd-7f86dd1d42f74fe2","cmd-c971142d7ad24a47","cmd-6064bc11fabe4072","cmd-b21aa62e4caa444b","cmd-aa5f389254f94282","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct state and cross-client behavioral evidence. The independent restart protocol is also complete for every managed node: each has a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered service, mount, identity, and data state. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently match the executor's post-restart identities, and a final write/read test demonstrates end-to-end operation after all three restarts.","limitations":[]}
